  "body": "First-stock evidence connects protected transport, observed placement, accepted handback and independently evaluated conventional completion. First-home clearing of the insert pad was insufficient for handback; retained controller state supports exhausted setup retries as the reason, followed by model-performed native setup and accepted transfer. Protected continuity after handback can lag the ownership transition because stale capabilities are denied; local notes and protected history retain reconciliation evidence, but no restart tested reuse. Stock02 generated one bounded public-history/status utility with admission and final receipts, not generated motor control. Home05 maximum journal lag occurred before model turn; stock05 late-continuity/closed-host transport association is an inference without exact failed-request linkage. These inspected mechanisms identify engineering questions, not controlled causal effects.",
